{
 "summary": "Checkout is failing because inventory POST /reserve became slow (p95 up to 4.77s) right after inventory was deployed from 3.1.5 to 3.2.1 at 07:18:17Z. Orders times out waiting on inventory and returns 504, and the gateway returns that to clients as 502. Inventory itself reports no 5xx; the errors show up in its callers.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory release 3.2.1, deployed at 07:18:17Z, made POST /reserve slow (most trace self time, ~2.4–2.6s). That slowness drives orders to time out with 504 and the gateway to return 502. The link to the deploy is timing (latency onset ~15–30s after it) plus all sampled slow traces running inventory 3.2.1. A code-level cause has not been confirmed, and inventory logs were unavailable.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-190058c637be",
   "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
   "ev-51525d7035d0",
   "ev-1da116a62fee",
   "ev-c000e6b4f684"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders appears to have a timeout shorter than inventory's latency. Orders returns 504 to the gateway, and gateway checkout traces fail at about 2.0–2.2s while inventory self time averages ~2.58s.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders 5xx ratio reached 100% (avg 47.9%), and gateway 5xx peaked at 71.8%. Inventory 5xx stayed at 0%, so the errors appear in the callers rather than in inventory.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-1da116a62fee",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684",
    "ev-51525d7035d0"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:17Z",
   "event": "Inventory deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1 by ci-pipeline",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:32.643000Z",
   "event": "Orders 5xx ratio crosses 5% and p95 latency crosses 1s",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:47.643000Z",
   "event": "Inventory p95 latency crosses 1s; gateway 5xx ratio and p95 latency cross their thresholds",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:20:33Z",
   "event": "Sampled traces show gateway 502 <- orders 504, with dominant self time in inventory POST /reserve (3.2.1)",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders is unlikely to be the origin. It reports 504s, but trace self time is concentrated in inventory POST /reserve, not in orders.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Gateway is unlikely to be the origin. Its 502s come from the downstream orders 504, and it was not deployed in the evidence.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A traffic surge is unlikely. Request rates stay low and steady (gateway ~2.1 rps avg, max 2.46).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c000e6b4f684",
    "ev-51525d7035d0"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Logs could not be queried (backend timeout), so there are no inventory application logs showing why /reserve is slow, such as lock contention, a slow DB query or an external dependency.",
  "No infrastructure or database metrics were provided for inventory's dependencies, so a coincident dependency problem cannot be excluded.",
  "The orders timeout to inventory is not given directly. It is only inferred as ~2s from trace durations.",
  "There is no trace or metric baseline from before the deploy on inventory 3.1.5 to compare latency against."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Roll inventory back from 3.2.1 to 3.1.5 and watch inventory p95 and orders/gateway 5xx ratios.",
   "rationale": "Latency began within ~30s of the deploy, and every slow trace has its dominant self time in inventory 3.2.1 POST /reserve. A rollback both mitigates the incident and tests the hypothesis.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be",
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-51525d7035d0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Re-run the log query for inventory (and orders) for 07:18–07:21 once the log backend responds.",
   "rationale": "Log collection failed. Inventory logs are needed to find what in 3.2.1 makes /reserve slow.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-logs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Review the 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1 diff for changes to the POST /reserve path, such as queries, locking or new downstream calls.",
   "rationale": "Self time is spent inside inventory POST /reserve itself.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-190058c637be"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Inspect example traces e1af7fdd63c588af3940a164158d28c1 and efc519b65a223a76d1b5de89ca1498b3 in Jaeger for child spans under /reserve.",
   "rationale": "This shows whether the time goes to internal work or to an uninstrumented dependency.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
